Only the decoders, apart from the system they run on: the media
frameworks CoreFoundation, CoreMedia, CoreVideo and CoreAudio are looked
for (and linked into libavutil) only with VideoToolbox or AudioToolbox,
which Minkar does not enable. Otherwise libavcodec would link Minkar's
CoreMedia, which uses it.

--- a/configure
+++ b/configure
@@ -7114,10 +7114,10 @@
 enabled metal        && check_apple_framework Metal
 enabled videotoolbox && check_apple_framework VideoToolbox
 
-check_apple_framework CoreFoundation
-check_apple_framework CoreMedia
-check_apple_framework CoreVideo
-check_apple_framework CoreAudio
+enabled videotoolbox && check_apple_framework CoreFoundation
+enabled videotoolbox && check_apple_framework CoreMedia
+enabled videotoolbox && check_apple_framework CoreVideo
+enabled audiotoolbox && check_apple_framework CoreAudio
 
 enabled audiotoolbox && {
     check_type AudioToolbox/AudioToolbox.h AudioObjectPropertyAddress
